Subject: [PATCH] fuzz: compile the parser regexes before the first input

The parser's regexes are private lazy_statics (src/parser.rs), compiled on
first use, so the first input of every fresh process paid for compiling all
of them (about 50x the cost of a typical input). Parse a fixed document that
uses each of them (line and block comment, single-quoted property name and
colon, double-quoted string) from a static constructor, so they are compiled
before the first input. Every input runs the same parser code as before; it
only no longer sees the one-time regex compilation. Related upstream:
google/json5format#38 / #47 (open, a fuzz_parse timeout in block comment
indentation, unrelated to this). Drop this patch if the regexes become
eagerly built or the fuzz target gets an init hook.

diff --git a/fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_parse.rs b/fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_parse.rs
index 35e3a7c..eb7764e 100644
--- a/fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_parse.rs
+++ b/fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_parse.rs
@@ -3,6 +3,18 @@ use libfuzzer_sys::fuzz_target;
 use json5format::*;
 use std::str;
 
+// The parser compiles its regexes lazily (private lazy_statics in src/parser.rs), on the
+// first parse. Parse a fixed document that uses every one of them from a static constructor,
+// so they are compiled before the first input instead of during it.
+#[used]
+#[link_section = ".init_array"]
+static INIT: extern "C" fn() = {
+    extern "C" fn init() {
+        let _ = ParsedDocument::from_str("// a\n/* b */\n{'c': \"d\"}", None);
+    }
+    init
+};
+
 fuzz_target!(|data: &[u8]| {
     if let Ok(utf8) = str::from_utf8(data) {
         ParsedDocument::from_str(utf8, None);
